place  those containment measures to slow the  spread  of the virus and that is a material  difference between us and the government  we would also by the way do more to  drive up vaccination rates amongst  younger people because we really need to  get younger people  uh to take part to take the vaccine and  of course  we would ask the speculation is the jcvi  are not going to propose  uh vaccination for adolescents we're  doing that in other countries  or they are doing it in other countries  in the united states in  in parts of europe and so on if that is  the advice from the jcpi then i suppose  that is the advice but i would really  ask them  to carefully consider whether or not we  should be vaccinating  uh teenage children in this country we  need to take another  a number of measures to really drive  infection rates down  stop people catching the viruses to stop  people being contacts of those  with the virus so just very briefly you  you are against vaccinating children  no no no i'm not against vaccinating  children i think it needs to be looked  at by  the jcpi if other countries are doing it  i don't understand why  we're not proposing it but of course in  the end these are always clinical  decisions  but if the jcvi are going to propose  tomorrow that  that we are that we should not vaccinate  children i hope they can fully explain  their thinking and why they've taken a  different decision to the united states  for example  thank you very much mr ashworth

